          "python",
          "Header guards (`#ifndef`, `#define`, `#endif`) prevent multiple inclusions of the same header, which would cause compiler errors.\n\n## Function Best Practices\n\n1. **Keep functions small and focused:** A function should do one thing well.\n2. **Use descriptive names:** Function names should indicate what they do.\n3. **Document parameters and return values:** Use comments to explain the interface.\n4. **Validate input:** Check preconditions and return error codes if necessary.\n5. **Avoid deep recursion:** Use iteration when possible.\n6. **Minimize side effects:** A function that only reads its parameters is easier to reason about than one that modifies global state."
        ]
